Soodeok Seo received his B.S. degree in the Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering at KAIST in 2019. He is currently a Ph.D. candidate in the Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering at KAIST under the direction of Prof. Bumjoon J. Kim. His present research interests are synthesis for organic conjugated materials of organic solar cells and device fabrication
Yun-Hi Kim is a professor in the Department of Chemistry at Gyeongsang National University. She received her Ph.D. degree from KAIST. Afterward she worked in MIT as a postdoc researcher. Her current research includes polymer designs for  the  development  of  high-performance  organic  light  emitting  diodes,  organic  photovoltaics,  organic  thin  film transistors, and organic photo diodes.
Bumjoon  J.  Kim is  a  KAIST  Endowed  Chair  Professor  and  Department  Head  in  the  Department  of  Chemical  and Biomolecular Engineering at KAIST. He received his Ph.D. degree from UC Santa Barbara under the guidance of Prof. Edward Kramer. Afterward he worked with Prof. Jean Fréchet at UC Berkeley as a postdoc researcher. His current research includes  polymer  designs  for  the  development  of  high-performance  and  mechanically-robust  solar  cells,  polymeric electrolyte  and  smart  responsive  block  copolymer-based  particles.  He  has  published  more  than  300  peer-reviewed papers and 70 patents.
